\n        <summary class=\"topic-summary\">\n            <span class=\"topic-title\">Created By</span>\n            <span class=\"topic-count\">1</span>\n        </summary>\n\n        \n        <div class=\"topic-examples\">\n            \n                <a\n                    href=\"/warhammer-40k/games-workshop\"\n                    class=\"connection\"\n                    data-relationship=\"Created By\"\n                >\n                    <strong>Games Workshop</strong>\n                    <span>Games Workshop, formally Games Workshop Group PLC (often abbreviated to GW), is a miniature wargaming company based in Nottingham in the United Kingdom and is the creator of the Warhammer,…</span>\n                </a>\n            \n        </div>\n        \n\n        <div class=\"topic-content\">\n            \n                <div class=\"fact-card\">\n                    <div class=\"fact-label\">\n                        Created By\n                    </div>\n\n                    <h3>\n        <a href=\"/warhammer-40k/games-workshop\" class=\"entity-link\">\n            Games Workshop\n        </a>\n    </h3>\n\n                    <p>Games Workshop publishes Warhammer 40,000.</p>\n\n                    \n\n                    \n                </div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </details>\n</section>\n\n</section>\n\n\n<section class=\"did-you-know\">\n    <h2>Did you know?</h2>\n    <ul>\n        <li>Warhammer 40,000 is also referenced as Warhammer 40K, 40K, WH40K.</li><li>Games Workshop publishes Warhammer 40,000.</li><li>The Imperium is central to Warhammer 40,000.</li><li>Warhammer 40,000 Video Games is a medium branch of Warhammer 40,000.</li><li>Warhammer 40,000 Tabletop is a medium branch of Warhammer 40,000.</li><li>Evidence around Warhammer 40,000 is classified as fiction on Ton-o-Lore.</li>\n    </ul>\n</section>\n\n\n<section class=\"sources\">\n    <h2>Sources &amp; further reading</h2>\n    <p><a href=\"https://warhammer40k.fandom.com/wiki/Warhammer_40,000\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Fandom wiki</a></p>\n</section>","overview":"<section class=\"overview\">\n    <h2>What is Warhammer 40,000?</h2>\n    \n    <p>\n        Warhammer 40,000 (informally known as Warhammer 40K, WH40K, W40K, or just 40K) is a science fantasy tabletop miniature wargame, produced by <a href=\"/warhammer-40k/games-workshop\" class=\"entity-link\">Games Workshop</a>.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        The intellectual property also has expanded in recent years to include other related tabletop miniature games, video games, novels, audiobooks, and animated features.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        Warhammer 40,000 is the science fantasy companion to the dark high fantasy world of Warhammer and [https://ageofsigmar.fandom.com/wiki/Age_of_Sigmar_Wiki Warhammer Age of Sigmar], and originally shared many of the same game mechanics and some of the setting elements with those properties.\n    </p>\n    <p>\n        The game depicts combat between the armies of the fictional universe of the 41st Millennium using 28 mm scale (approximately 1:65) miniature figurines which represent futuristic soldiers, creatures and vehicles of war.\n    </p>\n    \n    <p class=\"also-known-as\">\n        <strong>Also known as:</strong>\n        Warhammer 40K, 40K, WH40K, Warhammer 40000.\n    </p>\n\n</section>","word_count":839,"uniqueness_score":"1.0000"},"entity":{"id":"5337e51c-272b-4f2d-8238-13117fcfcf60","name":"Warhammer 40,000","slug":"warhammer-40k","type":"topic","kind":"topic","type_label":"Topic","short_description":"Warhammer 40,000 (informally known as Warhammer 40K, WH40K, W40K, or just 40K) is a science fantasy tabletop miniature wargame, produced by Games Workshop.","description":"Warhammer 40,000 (informally known as Warhammer 40K, WH40K, W40K, or just 40K) is a science fantasy tabletop miniature wargame, produced by Games Workshop.\n\nThe intellectual property also has expanded in recent years to include other related tabletop miniature games, video games, novels, audiobooks, and animated features.\n\nWarhammer 40,000 is the science fantasy companion to the dark high fantasy world of Warhammer and [https://ageofsigmar.fandom.com/wiki/Age_of_Sigmar_Wiki Warhammer Age of Sigmar], and originally shared many of the same game mechanics and some of the setting elements with those properties.\n\nThe game depicts combat between the armies of the fictional universe of the 41st Millennium using 28 mm scale (approximately 1:65) miniature figurines which represent futuristic soldiers, creatures and vehicles of war.","evidence":"fiction","universe":"warhammer-40k","aliases":["Warhammer 40K","40K","WH40K","Warhammer 40000"],"wikipedia_url":null,"image_url":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/warhammer40k/images/5/5f/Warhammer_40%2C000-_The_New_Edition_Cinematic_Trailer/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/360?cb=20240712152901","image_source":"https://warhammer40k.fandom.com/wiki/Warhammer_40,000","image_credit":"Fair-use identification thumbnail via Fandom. Character / franchise art © Games Workshop (as applicable). Not free or redistributable artwork.","image_license":"fair_use","image_usage":"fair_use_identification","image_alt":"Identification thumbnail for Warhammer 40,000"},"connections":[],"rabbit_holes":[],"copyright":{"theme":"warhammer-40k","title":"Warhammer 40,000 is not owned by Ton-o-Lore.","body":"Warhammer 40,000, Warhammer, the Imperium of Man, Space Marines, Chaos, and related characters, artwork, logos, and intellectual property are the property of Games Workshop Limited and other credited rights holders. Ton-o-Lore is an independent, unofficial fan and informational project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Games Workshop or those rights holders. Identification logos and thumbnails, when shown, are low-resolution images used under a fair-use rationale for commentary and identification only — not free or redistributable artwork."},"subject":{"id":"warhammer-40k","name":"Wa